# Sovereign audit ledger (append-only, host-owned, may contain sensitive action detail)
# The arsenal's SOURCE assets live under data/ and must be tracked, so the blanket
# ignore is narrowed to data/* and the source files are re-included explicitly.
# (A bare "data/" cannot be negated: git refuses to descend into an ignored directory.)
data/*
!data/.gitignore
!data/arsenal_fewshot.jsonl
!data/arsenal/
data/arsenal/*
!data/arsenal/feeds/
!data/arsenal/feeds/**
!data/arsenal/ids/
!data/arsenal/ids/**
!data/arsenal/wordlists/
!data/arsenal/wordlists/**
# Arsenal runtime OUTPUT (quarantine copies and forensic captures) is never source.
data/arsenal/quarantine/
data/arsenal/forensics/

# ============================================================
# QUARANTINE GUARD — the quarantine itself lives OUTSIDE this repo
# Chain Key: 360ea36c28e66d9d
#
# The quarantine root is  C:\Users\AA5II\kali\qui\
#   ├── .env.bak-*        rotated/retired credential snapshots, revoked
#   └── bun.lock          isolated divergent lockfile (Gate 5 blocker)
#
# It was briefly placed INSIDE this repository, then moved back out: a tree of
# live credentials is not a safe resident of a directory tree that gets cloned,
# archived, zipped, and scanned by every tool that walks the workspace. Keeping
# it outside removes an entire class of accidental disclosure instead of
# guarding against it with ignore rules.
#
# The rule below is therefore a BACKSTOP, not the primary defence. If a copy of
# that directory ever reappears here, git will still refuse to stage it.
# ============================================================
kali/
kali/**
kali/qui/

# Upstream's bare `secrets/` rule (above) matches at ANY depth, so it also swallowed
# src/neo/arsenal/secrets/ - the secrets-scanner MODULE. The rule is meant for a
# top-level credentials directory; the module is source and must be committed.
!src/neo/arsenal/secrets/

